From fcd326be7c673f3db5e3098181f8ce76e8a290d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:47:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci-review comment: wall-clock retry budget, one
 re-refresh per head (PR #1699 review nits 2, 3)

Nit 2: the "~90 s" retry budget counted only sleeps; each failed artifact
attempt can also spend its archive-API (30 s) and blob (60 s) timeouts, so a
delayed re-refresh (300 s wait + 6 x 90 s + 90 s) or a sweep during an
artifact outage (65 PRs) could run past timeout-minutes: 15 and be cancelled.
Every run now has a wall-clock budget from the start of main() (RUN_BUDGET_S =
JOB_TIMEOUT_S - 180 s headroom, the re-refresh delay included): a retry, a
further artifact or a further PR starts only if a full attempt
(DOWNLOAD_ATTEMPT_MAX_S, derived from the two timeouts) still fits, so the run
ends red with a log line instead of being cancelled.

Nit 3: a failed refresh queued a re-refresh even when it kept the head's
completed "ran on" snapshot, and once per failed CI- or Docker-triggered run.
mark_refresh_failed now reads the PR and comment first and queues nothing when
the marker is skipped (closed/moved head, newer snapshot, completed snapshot
kept); a queued re-refresh is recorded in the state line (requeued=), carried
through later failed marks of that head, and dropped by a successful snapshot,
so CI + Docker failures on one head queue one.

Card t_01a1d1827d121b26. Review: PR #1699 review 5880960246.
